      "field": "national_digits",
      "web_behaviour": "checkout.wajub keeps the 0 the payer typed, and gives it back to a number typed without it only when that makes a mobile number (CI 01, 05, 07; BJ 01 2[5-9], 01 [4-69]): 0303000000 and 0130000000 are accepted, 303000000 and 130000000 refused.",
      "why_mobile_differs": "national_digits drops every leading 0 (the shared algorithm), so each pair reads the same and both are accepted; api.wajub decides on such a number either way."
    },
